  "id": "ghb",
  "term": "GHB",
  "definition": "GHB is a naturally present fatty acid in the body, especially in the brain, that serves as a precursor to GABA. It acts on GHB receptors and somewhat on GABA-B receptors, influences several brain chemical systems, and mainly slows central nervous system activity, giving it neuromodulatory and anesthetic effects.",
